Original commit body from e333877f0bfd7fd6a22c200afa0245c3fa79cda0:

_wait_for_modal polled up to 30 event-loop ticks for a widget to appear and then
RETURNED AS THOUGH IT HAD SUCCEEDED. Every caller then drove a DOM that was not
ready and failed later with an assertion about a RESULT --
`assert 'NOT_SET' is None`, the _ModalTestApp._capture sentinel -- naming neither
the widget nor the wait.

That is the failure that took the 2026-08-20 13:00 full-suite cron red on
TestLockScreenUnit::test_cancel_returns_none. Because Woodpecker collapses a
workflow's steps into one aggregate commit status, it made self-claims-gate,
self-tree-validation and test-agent-infra unreadable alongside it for as long as
it stayed red -- which is the masking INV-bozid is filed on. This does not
satisfy that item's statement; it removes its live cause.

TWO CHANGES.

1. IT RAISES ON EXHAUSTION, naming what it waited for and for how long. A helper
   that gives up quietly is a green tick over a hole -- the same note this repo
   already writes about a skip that can be reached by a typo.

2. IT WAITS FOR LAYOUT, NOT MERE DOM PRESENCE. pilot.click(selector) resolves the
   widget's screen region and synthesises a mouse event at its centre, so a
   widget that is in the DOM but not yet laid out has a zero-sized region: the
   click lands nowhere, no button is pressed, and the dismiss callback never
   runs. That is exactly the observed symptom, and presence-is-not-reachability
   is the same distinction the io-boundary work keeps paying for.

NOT REPRODUCIBLE LOCALLY, and that is stated rather than worked around: five
consecutive runs of the modal/screen classes pass, 60 each in ~22s. It fits a CI
run carrying 23,210 tests under load and does not fit a deterministic bug. So the
fix is argued from the mechanism and pinned by a test that drives the helper at a
widget which will never appear, plus a POSITIVE CONTROL that the happy path still
returns -- without which the cheapest way to pass the first test is a helper that
always raises, a different bug with the same cost.

556 tracker tests green.

